    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt5}{2}$.\n\nUse corresponding long and short sides: $x=\\dfrac1{x-1}$.",
      "worked": "The remaining rectangle has sides $1$ and $x-1$. Corresponding long and short sides give\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{1}&=\\frac{1}{x-1}\\\\x(x-1)&=1\\\\x^2-x&=1\\\\x^2-x+\\frac14&=1+\\frac14\\\\\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)^2&=\\frac54\\\\x-\\frac12&=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince removing the square requires $x>1$, $x=\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt5}{2}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 90
